Here's a solution for your problem using TypedArray and Bitwise operations:

```javascript
function packEntities(entities) {
  const buffer = new Uint16Array(Math.ceil(entities.length / 2));

  let offset = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < entities.length; i++) {
    const entity = entities[i];
    const id = entity.id & 0xF; // masking to get 4 bits
    const size = (entity.size & 0x7) << 3; // shifting and masking to get 3 bits

    buffer[offset] = (id << 12) | (size << 9); // packing id and size
    offset++;
  }

  return buffer.buffer;
}

function unpackEntities(buffer, length) {
  const entities = [];
  const view = new DataView(buffer);

  for (let i = 0; i < length; i += 2) {
    const word = view.getUint16(i);
    const id = (word >> 12) & 0xF; // masking to get 4 bits
    const size = (word >> 9) & 0x7; // masking to get 3 bits

    entities.push({ id, size });
  }

  return entities;
}
```

In the `packEntities` function, we create a Uint16Array buffer and pack the entities into it using bitwise operations. The id and size are packed into a single 16-bit word.

In the `unpackEntities` function, we create a DataView from the buffer and unpack the entities from it using bitwise operations. The id and size are extracted from each 16-bit word.

